h.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 09-10-2022, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T15:53:19-07:00","id":1550862,"title":"","content":"After playing with some of the rule tweaks in this thread for I while (after an initial rule change to S20, mostly), I wanted to note down how they were received by the players and how they have impacted the game.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspects:</b><br /> We're using the simplified list I made on the first page. Every Path uses a Primary Aspect, which determines the Casting Level and difficulty of the spell. This works rather well, especially consolidating the Aspects that are Space and Mass in some form or another keeps looking up the table for reference when needed short. The S20 system didn't work out for us, at all. We switched back to Revised rules for a while, but being able to use Auxiliary Aspects for all Paths when appropriate was fun, so that went back in.<br /> <br /> <b>Extra Successes:</b><br /> Without doubt, rolling first and <i>then</i> spend extra successes on Aspects was the single best tweak. Casting spells is less frustrating, and the Sorcerers actually want to use Sorcery (people using the all-or-nothing rule will know what that means).<br /> <br /> <b>Casting Time:</b><br /> This one changed a lot. I completely ignored longer casting times for higher level spells at the start, but we eventually settled on kind of the reverse: It takes one round to cast a spell (effect roll is resolved in the second round), but for every additional round spent on casting, the Sorcerer can reduce the difficulty of the spell by one. This makes casting high-level spells in combat actually somewhat viable or at least worth the investment. We bumped up basic casting difficulty to Casting Level +5 in exchange.<br /> <br /> <b>Mana/Techn\u00e9:</b><br /> <i>All</i> Sorcerers in the group use this Background, and I allowed using Quintessence instead of Willpower for casting. Naturally, this is always the preferred resource for casting before touching Willpower. Actually, if I had a new player join the group I would be tempted to make a Quintessence pool a default stat for sorcerers and use Willpower as most other splats do. I however don't like making Meditation (to regain QE) a 'must pick' skill, so I'm thinking about using a Focus roll (Attribute + Ability) would be better instead: the character spends time researching or practicing their arts.<br /> <br /> <b>Rituals:</b><br /> To put it bluntly, my players do not like to invest XP to buy Rituals nor the time investment necessary to make their own Rituals. XP and downtime are rather invested into Paths, Attributes, Abilities, or Willpower. While I get the priorities, I want to make Rituals a larger part of the game because they are fun. I'm interested if STs have found a good way to make Rituals more attractive, and creating them less of a chore. Maybe something like making them usable rather early (Cast Path as Ritual), but more refined/effective over time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://